  <Template Id="10006">
    <Name>* Simplified Citations Master Template   </Name>
    <Description>(NOTE: All other templates using simplified citations should start with this one. Items may be REMOVED from copies of this template to create other ones but NOTHING should be added to those templates unless it is also added here.)

This template is designed to make citing sources consistent across many types of records (for example, books, gravestones, and wedding certificates, etc.). The fields are populated with information based upon the type of source they represent: traditional or non-traditional. Traditional sources are those usually found in bibliographies and reference lists (e.g., books, periodicals, newspapers, etc.). Non-traditional sources include most everything else: birth certificates. cemetery records, census records, gravestones, photographs, social security records, etc.

Fields that generally refer to traditional sources are indicated with an asterisk (*). In the event that information is entered into related fields for both traditional and non-traditional sources (such as author and primary creator), the template will usually give preference to the traditional field during output. This should help eliminate redundancy within the citation.

This custom template and the citation style it uses was created by Jeff La Marca.</Description>
    <Category>Simplified Citations for Genealogical Sources</Category>
    <Footnote>&lt;[Author:Reverse]&lt;, [Role]&gt;|[PrimaryCreator]&lt;,  [Department]&gt;&gt; &lt;?[BookTitle][Title]|([Date])|([Date])&gt;. &lt;?[BookTitle][Title]|&lt; &quot;[Title]&gt;&lt;?[Title]|&lt;,&quot; &lt;i&gt;[BookTitle]&lt;? [BookTitle]|&lt;: [Subtitle]&gt;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&gt;|&lt; &lt;i&gt;[BookTitle]&lt;? [BookTitle]|&lt;: [Subtitle]&gt;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&gt;&gt;&lt;?[BookTitle]|.|.&quot;&gt;|&lt;?[SourceDescription]|[SourceDescription:Caps]&lt;: [Person]&gt;.|&lt; [Person].&gt;&gt;&gt;&lt;?[BookTitle][Title]|&lt; [PublishLocation]&gt;&lt;: [Publisher]&gt;&lt;?[Publisher]|.|&gt;&gt; ||&lt; [Page].&gt;&lt; [SourceDetailPerson].&gt;&lt; [Location]&gt;&lt;&lt;; enumeration district [CensusED]&gt;&lt;, [HouseholdID]&gt;&gt;&lt;?[Location]|.&gt;&lt;&lt; [Repository:Caps]&gt;&lt;?[Repository]|&lt; ([URL]&gt;&lt;? [URL]|&lt;: accessed [Accessed]&gt;&gt;&lt;?[URL]|)&gt;.&gt;&gt;&lt; [RefNumber:Caps].&gt;</Footnote>
    <ShortFootnote>&lt;[Author:Reverse]&lt;, [Role]&gt;|[PrimaryCreator]&lt;,  [Department]&gt;&gt; &lt;?[BookTitle][Title]|([Date])|([Date])&gt;. &lt;?[BookTitle][Title]|&lt; &quot;[Title]&gt;&lt;?[Title]|&lt;,&quot; &lt;i&gt;[BookTitle]&lt;? [BookTitle]|&lt;: [Subtitle]&gt;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&gt;|&lt; &lt;i&gt;[BookTitle]&lt;? [BookTitle]|&lt;: [Subtitle]&gt;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&gt;&gt;&lt;?[BookTitle]|.|.&quot;&gt;|&lt;?[SourceDescription]|[SourceDescription:Caps]&lt;: [Person]&gt;.|&lt; [Person].&gt;&gt;&gt;</ShortFootnote>
    <Bibliography>&lt;[Author:Reverse]&lt;, [Role]&gt;|[PrimaryCreator]&lt;,  [Department]&gt;&gt; &lt;?[BookTitle][Title]|([Date])|([Date])&gt;. &lt;?[BookTitle][Title]|&lt; &quot;[Title]&gt;&lt;?[Title]|&lt;,&quot; &lt;i&gt;[BookTitle]&lt;? [BookTitle]|&lt;: [Subtitle]&gt;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&gt;|&lt; &lt;i&gt;[BookTitle]&lt;? [BookTitle]|&lt;: [Subtitle]&gt;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&gt;&gt;&lt;?[BookTitle]|.|.&quot;&gt;|&lt;?[SourceDescription]|[SourceDescription:Caps]&lt;: [Person]&gt;.|&lt; [Person].&gt;&gt;&gt;&lt;?[BookTitle][Title]|&lt; [PublishLocation]&gt;&lt;: [Publisher]&gt;&lt;?[Publisher]|.|&gt;&gt; ||&lt; [Page].&gt;&lt; [SourceDetailPerson].&gt;&lt; [Location]&gt;&lt;&lt;; enumeration district [CensusED]&gt;&lt;, [HouseholdID]&gt;&gt;&lt;?[Location]|.&gt;&lt;&lt; [Repository:Caps]&gt;&lt;?[Repository]|&lt; ([URL]&gt;&lt;? [URL]|&lt;: accessed [Accessed]&gt;&gt;&lt;?[URL]|)&gt;.&gt;&gt;&lt; [RefNumber:Caps].&gt;</Bibliography>
    <Field>
      <Type>Name</Type>
      <Name>PrimaryCreator</Name>
      <Display>Primary Creator</Display>
      <Hint>i.e., Bellevue Hospital for the Criminally Insane, End of the Road Cemetery, California, etc.</Hint>
      <Detail>False</Detail>
      <LongHint>List the agency, organization, state, or other entity that created and/or has sole responsibility for maintenance of this source.

Examples might include the names of:

    cemetery,
    church,
    hospital, 
    mortuary,
    school,
    state or other large government entity.

In the event that one or more individuals names are listed here (for example the name of a photographer or the writer of a letter), the following format should be used:

    1 name:  Doe, John (list surnmame first)
    2 names: Doe, John and John Brown
    3 or more names: Doe, John; John Brown; and Susy Smith</LongHint>
    </Field>
    <Field>
      <Type>Text</Type>
      <Name>Department</Name>
      <Display>Dept. or Office</Display>
      <Hint>Department of Vital Statistics, Department of Motor Vehicles, etc.</Hint>
      <Detail>False</Detail>
      <LongHint>Optional field. Some sources come from very large entities (esp. govermental records). Examples might be Dept. of Vital Records or Dept. of Motor Vehicles.</LongHint>
    </Field>
    <Field>
      <Type>Name</Type>
      <Name>Author</Name>
      <Display>Author(s)/Editor(s)*</Display>
      <Hint>name of author(s) or editor(s). refer to hints for info on entering more than one name</Hint>
      <Detail>False</Detail>
      <LongHint>Use this field only if document or source comes from an item that could be used in a traditional biblography or reference list. If more than one name is provided, they should be should be entered into this field with a semicolon (so that they&apos;ll be formatted properly in citations. For example, if three names are to be listed, they should be entered as:

     John Brown; John Doe; Susy Smith

In the event that the name of an agency or other organization is entered, it should be enclosed in forward slashes (/) so that it will be displayed properly in the citation, for example:

/Wall Street Journal/</LongHint>
    </Field>
    <Field>
      <Type>Text</Type>
      <Name>Role</Name>
      <Display>Role*</Display>
      <Hint>e.g., compiler, editor, transcriber, translator</Hint>
      <Detail>False</Detail>
      <LongHint>This is an optional field that is used to indicate the person(s) played a role other than that of an author.</LongHint>
    </Field>
    <Field>
      <Type>Date</Type>
      <Name>Date</Name>
      <Display>Date</Display>
      <Hint>date created, issued, or published</Hint>
      <Detail>False</Detail>
      <LongHint>Enter the date when this source was created, initially indexed, or first came into being.</LongHint>
    </Field>
    <Field>
      <Type>Text</Type>
      <Name>BookTitle</Name>
      <Display>Source/Book Title*</Display>
      <Hint>Enter name of book, newspaper, periodical, etc.</Hint>
      <Detail>False</Detail>
      <LongHint>Optional field. Use only if source is an item that can be used in a traditional biblography or reference list. </LongHint>
    </Field>
    <Field>
      <Type>Text</Type>
      <Name>Subtitle</Name>
      <Display>Source Subtitle*</Display>
      <Hint/>
      <Detail>False</Detail>
      <LongHint>This is an optional field. Enter name of the book&apos;s subtitle if one exists.</LongHint>
    </Field>
    <Field>
      <Type>Text</Type>
      <Name>Title</Name>
      <Display>Title*</Display>
      <Hint>Specific article, document, or chapter title</Hint>
      <Detail>False</Detail>
      <LongHint>Optional field. Use only if document or source comes from an item that can be used in a traditional biblography or reference list. 

The specific name of the article, chapter, or other title should be entered.
</LongHint>
    </Field>
    <Field>
      <Type>Text</Type>
      <Name>SourceDescription</Name>
      <Display>Source Description</Display>
      <Hint>Title or description of document</Hint>
      <Detail>False</Detail>
      <LongHint>Used for documents and sources where a person or persons name are the main topic. 

Examples:

   Birth Certificate
   Diploma
   Golf Club Membership Card
   Headstone
   Letter (or Personal Correspondence)
   Marriage Certificate
   Passsenger Ship List, S.S. Trojan Prince
   Photograph
   1880 U.S. Census

Use &quot;title casing&quot; for capitalization. The field should be kept as generic as possible. A few sources may require clarification. For example, passenger ship records should list the name of the ship. Date or other very specific information should not be included except for cenus records (the year distinguishes one census from another).</LongHint>
    </Field>
    <Field>
      <Type>Text</Type>
      <Name>Person</Name>
      <Display>Person(s) of Interest</Display>
      <Hint>John Doe, Jane Smith, Doe Family, etc.</Hint>
      <Detail>False</Detail>
      <LongHint>If this source refers to a specific individual, list his or her name.

If two individuals are list and are of equal primary importance to the source (e.g., a wedding couple), list as: Ralph Brown and Jane Doe

If this source refers to a group of individuals of primary interest, list by family names (e.g. Brown Family, Smith Family, Brown and Smith Families), or by group (e.g., Doe cousins, Smalltown Bowling Club, Boy Scouts from Troop XYZ, etc.).</LongHint>
    </Field>
    <Field>
      <Type>Text</Type>
      <Name>Publisher</Name>
      <Display>Publisher*</Display>
      <Hint>Name of publisher (traditional sources only)</Hint>
      <Detail>False</Detail>
      <LongHint>Optional field - used only to list names of traditional publishers - books, magazines, newspapers, etc.</LongHint>
    </Field>
    <Field>
      <Type>Text</Type>
      <Name>PublishLocation</Name>
      <Display>Publish. Location*</Display>
      <Hint>List city and state (or city and country)</Hint>
      <Detail>False</Detail>
      <LongHint>Used only for traditional sources (e.g., books, newspapers, periodicals).

Location where item was published, printed, or created.</LongHint>
    </Field>
    <Field>
      <Type>Text</Type>
      <Name>Page</Name>
      <Display>Page Number(s)</Display>
      <Hint>p. 25, pp. 52, sheet B-4, etc.</Hint>
      <Detail>True</Detail>
      <LongHint>If the document has a page number, list it here.

Found in traditional and non-traditional sources.</LongHint>
    </Field>
    <Field>
      <Type>Name</Type>
      <Name>SourceDetailPerson</Name>
      <Display>Person</Display>
      <Hint>enter name of individual (refer to hint for details on when to use)</Hint>
      <Detail>True</Detail>
      <LongHint>This is an optional element and should only be used if more than one person&apos;s name (or that of a group) is listed on the master source. This element is also used to recognize the person&apos;s inclusion in a book or periodical..</LongHint>
    </Field>
    <Field>
      <Type>Place</Type>
      <Name>Location</Name>
      <Display>Location</Display>
      <Hint>e.g., city, county, state, country</Hint>
      <Detail>True</Detail>
      <LongHint>Provide location where source was created (if not mentioned above), it&apos;s physical location (e.g., grave site), or where the event occurred (locatation of baptism, place of census, marriage location, etc.)</LongHint>
    </Field>
    <Field>
      <Type>Text</Type>
      <Name>CensusED</Name>
      <Display>Census Enum. Dist.</Display>
      <Hint>e.g. 25</Hint>
      <Detail>True</Detail>
      <LongHint/>
    </Field>
    <Field>
      <Type>Text</Type>
      <Name>HouseholdID</Name>
      <Display>Census House. ID</Display>
      <Hint>dwelling 245, family 123</Hint>
      <Detail>True</Detail>
      <LongHint>Optional. Used only for census records.</LongHint>
    </Field>
    <Field>
      <Type>Text</Type>
      <Name>Repository</Name>
      <Display>Repository</Display>
      <Hint>i.e., Ancestry.com, National Archives and Records Administration, etc.</Hint>
      <Detail>True</Detail>
      <LongHint>This field should only be used for hard-to-find, one-of-a-kind documents, or individually held sources. If this source was found on the Internet, then the name of the web site should be listed here. This is an OPTIONAL field and should not be used for traditional materials (books, articles, etc.) that can easily be found using standard reference search techniques (such as looking through a library card catalog).

Examples:

    Ancestry.com
    National Archives and Records Administration

In the event that there is just one known copy of a source (and it is unlikely that other copies exist), state:

    &quot;privately held by [name of owner]&quot;

If an individual has possession of a source and that other copies of that source may exist (although locating these copies would be difficult, if not impossible), state:

    &quot;copy in possession of [name of owner]&quot;</LongHint>
    </Field>
    <Field>
      <Type>Text</Type>
      <Name>URL</Name>
      <Display>URL</Display>
      <Hint>http://www.ancestry.com</Hint>
      <Detail>True</Detail>
      <LongHint>Provide the address of the home page of the website where this document was found (optional - list the full path to the document but remember that this will not always remain the same and, dependent upon the web site, is also subject to change).</LongHint>
    </Field>
    <Field>
      <Type>Date</Type>
      <Name>Accessed</Name>
      <Display>Date File Accessed</Display>
      <Hint>enter the date this source was accessed or viewed</Hint>
      <Detail>True</Detail>
      <LongHint>In the event that this source was found online, enter the date it was viewed.</LongHint>
    </Field>
    <Field>
      <Type>Text</Type>
      <Name>RefNumber</Name>
      <Display>Misc. Ref. Num.</Display>
      <Hint>&quot;document # 123&quot;, &quot;case # 456&quot;, etc.</Hint>
      <Detail>True</Detail>
      <LongHint>Optional field, use only if absolutely necessary to locate document.

Examples of numbers that might be included here are:

driver license
Social Security number
Grave plot number
Passport number</LongHint>
    </Field>
    <Field>
      <Type>Text</Type>
      <Name>PersonalID</Name>
      <Display>Personal ID</Display>
      <Hint>e.g. STGe0123</Hint>
      <Detail>True</Detail>
      <LongHint>Copies of EVERYTHING should be kept. List your personal Library Document ID number here (use whatever numbering/cataloging method you like, just be consistent).</LongHint>
    </Field>
  </Template>
</SourceTemplates>
